SUMMARY:The Social Set: Padel & Pickleball 
LOCATION:Offsite: 25 Pier 4 Blvd.\, Boston
DESCRIPTION:Category: Sports & Games\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 11 spots l
 eft\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/206904\n\n2:00PM Pro-Led Instruction\, 2:30PM Open Play\, 4:00PM - Re
 covery and Member Mingling\n\nJoin us for an offsite afternoon of play as 
 The 'Quin House takes over the courts at Ballers in the Seaport. Whether y
 ou're picking up the racquet for the first time\, or have tried the sport 
 and would like to learn more\, members are invited to experience two of t
 oday’s most exciting racquet sports\, pickleball and padel\, in a lively
 \, social setting.\n\nThe afternoon will begin with professional instructo
 rs Mike Millet for pickleball and Colin Lamusta for padel\, giving member
 s guidance before moving into rotating play and friendly matches across bo
 th sports\, guided by the Ballers team. Members will have the opportunity 
 to rotate between pickleball and padel courts to experience both racquet s
 ports with pros and members. Post play\, members can stick around to mix\,
  mingle\, and enjoy food and drinks for purchase at the Ballers food truck
 s and bar. After play\, members are welcome to stick around to mix\, ming
 le\, and enjoy food and drinks available for purchase from the Ballers foo
 d trucks and bar.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members
  only. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 48 hours prio
 r to the start of the event.
