SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: From Head Of The Charles to Los Angeles 2028 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: Sports & Games\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 98 spots l
 eft\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.co
 m/events/206907\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\n\nAs the rowing 
 world turns its attention to Boston for one of the sport’s most celebrat
 ed weekends\, join us for a timely ’Quin Chat with NBC10 Boston Host Han
 nah Donnelly and two-time Olympic rower and Massachusetts native\, Kristi 
 Wagner. Fresh off competing at the World Rowing Championships\, Wagner wil
 l share an inside look at her experience on the international stage\, the 
 training and determination required to compete among the world’s best\, 
 and what comes next as she sets her sights on earning another Olympic bert
 h for the Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games.\n\nTogether\, Donnelly and Wagne
 r will dive into the excitement surrounding this year’s Head Of The Char
 les Regatta\, where Wagner will once again take to the water\, and explore
  what makes the iconic race such a defining moment for Boston and the glob
 al rowing community. Their conversation will also take a broader look at t
 he state of U.S. women’s rowing\, the athletes and momentum shaping its 
 future\, and the road ahead as the sport builds toward Los Angeles in 2028
 . From racing on the Charles to competing on the world’s biggest stage\,
  the evening offers a rare glimpse into the life of an elite athlete and t
 he ambition\, preparation\, and perseverance behind the pursuit of Olympic
  excellence.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only
 . Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask
  that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of th
 e event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206907
CATEGORIES:Sports & Games
END:VEVENT
