BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206906@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T193000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Starting Over with John and Yoko" with Roger Farringt
 on and Kenneth Womack
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 48 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/206906\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\n\nFresh off the book’
 s launch in New York City\, join us for Boston’s exclusive first look at
  “Starting Over with John and Yoko”\, featuring Boston-based photograp
 her Roger Farrington and renowned Beatles historian and author Kenneth Wom
 ack. The book transports readers back to August 7th\, 1980\, when John Len
 non and Yoko Ono returned to the recording studio after a five-year absenc
 e to begin work on what would become “Double Fantasy”. Farrington\, th
 en an up-and-coming photographer\, was given the assignment of a lifetime:
  capture the image that would announce Lennon’s return to music. Just fo
 ur months later\, Lennon’s assassination would transform those photograp
 hs into a poignant record of one of music history’s final chapters.\n\nI
 n conversation\, Farrington and Womack will take members inside Manhattan�
 ��s Hit Factory and behind the images from that extraordinary day\, sharin
 g the stories and circumstances surrounding a moment few could have known 
 would become so significant. Featuring the complete collection of Farringt
 on’s photographs from the session for the first time\, “Starting Over 
 with John and Yoko” also offers a fascinating glimpse into celebrity pho
 tography in the pre-digital era. Drawing on Farrington’s decades photogr
 aphing some of the world’s most recognizable figures and Womack’s exte
 nsive scholarship on the Beatles and John Lennon\, the conversation will e
 xplore photography\, music\, memory\, and the enduring cultural legacy of 
 Lennon and Ono.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members o
 nly. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly 
 ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of
  the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206906
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
