SUMMARY:Fashion Salon: An Evening with MONSE
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206908\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6
 :30PM Programming\, 7:30PM Boutique Shopping\nJoin us for an immersive fas
 hion salon with MONSE\, the New York–based fashion house known for its d
 econstructed tailoring\, unexpected proportions\, and singular take on mod
 ern femininity. Co-Founder and Co-Creative Director Fernando Garcia will p
 resent the Fall/Winter 2026 collection\, salon style and share the inspira
 tions\, craftsmanship\, and stories behind some of the season’s most dis
 tinctive pieces\, offering members a rare glimpse into his creative proces
 s. In a nod to the intimate maison presentations that helped shape the mod
 ern runway\, models will move throughout The Reading Room\, inviting membe
 rs to settle in\, relax\, and experience the collection up close.\n\nAt th
 e heart of the collection is the sunflower\, hand-painted by Garcia and re
 imagined as a symbol of resilience\, longevity\, and enduring vitality. Th
 e motif appears throughout in rich shades of marigold\, burgundy\, red\, b
 rown\, and grey\, across fluid silks\, intricate embroidery\, dimensional 
 knits\, deconstructed tailoring\, and sculptural eveningwear.\n\nFollowing
  the presentation\, members are invited to continue the evening in The Ter
 race with an exclusive MONSE shopping experience and the opportunity to ex
 plore the collection firsthand with the MONSE team.\n\n*This event is comp
 limentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and ref
 reshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at 
 least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206908
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
