BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206916@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Wealth\, Well Lived
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 110 spots le
 ft\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /206916\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nWhat does it really mean 
 to live a wealthy life? In the first of a new\, multi-part series presente
 d with Willow and The Impact Collective we will look beyond what we earn\
 , save\, or invest\, to consider how wealth reflects the choices we make\,
  the opportunities we create\, and the values we carry into our personal a
 nd professional lives. Joined by Lacy Garcia\, Founder and CEO of Willow\,
  and Julia Johannsen\, Founder and Executive Director of The Impact Collec
 tive\, this discussion will explore the intersection of money\, investing\
 , and personal values. Together\, they will begin to decode the systems th
 at shape our financial lives and consider how greater understanding can le
 ad to more informed\, purposeful decisions. As the series unfolds\, expect
  to explore conversations such as the wealth gap\, generational planning\,
  roles and representation\, and the ways we can rethink traditional ideas 
 of wealth to better align our investments with the lives and\, legacies we
  want to build.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members o
 nly. Complimentary light bites will be served\, with beverages available f
 or purchase throughout the evening. We kindly ask that all cancellations b
 e made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206916
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-207953@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261029T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261029T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261029T171500
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker: Jefferson's Bourbon | Session I
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 50 spots 
 left\nStatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/207953\n\nJoin us for an intimate tasting experience with Jefferson’s
  Bourbon\, exploring the craftsmanship\, character\, and creativity behind
  each pour. The evening begins with a welcome cocktail and time to mingle 
 before a guided tasting led by Jefferson’s founder Trey Zoeller. A Kentu
 cky native with deep family ties to American whiskey\, Zoeller founded Jef
 ferson’s with his father in 1997 and has become known for challenging bo
 urbon tradition through inventive approaches to aging and blending\, earni
 ng him a place in the Kentucky Bourbon Hall of Fame.\n\nAs straight tastin
 g pours are passed\, Trey will share the story of Jefferson’s while guid
 ing members through the flavor profiles\, production process\, and distinc
 tive character of each selection. Following the tasting\, the evening open
 s back up for conversation\, giving members the opportunity to mingle\, re
 visit their favorites\, and connect with Trey one-on-one for questions and
  a deeper dive into the world of Jefferson’s Bourbon.\n\n*This event is 
 complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and
  refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made
  at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/207953
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
